# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# |<---- 72 chars max ---->|
#
# Types (STRICT — no other types allowed):
#   feat     — new feature (MINOR bump)
#   fix      — bug fix (PATCH bump)
#   docs     — documentation only
#   style    — formatting, no logic change (prettier, etc.)
#   refactor — code change, no feat/fix
#   perf     — performance improvement
#   test     — add/correct tests
#   build    — build system or external deps
#   ci       — CI configuration
#   chore    — maintenance, no prod change
#   revert   — revert prior commit
#
# Scopes (STRICT — use one of these):
#   agent, browser, hud, server, stt, planner, verifier, loop,
#   highlight, ws, config, deps, docs, repo, ci, release
#
# Rules (enforced by commitlint):
#   - type is required, lowercase
#   - scope is required, lowercase (enables changelog per module)
#   - subject: imperative, lowercase start, no period, <=72 chars
#   - body: wrap at 100 chars, explain WHAT + WHY (not HOW)
#   - footer: BREAKING CHANGE: <description> or Closes #<issue>
#
# Examples:
#   feat(hud): add interrupt button with abort controller
#   fix(planner): handle zod parse failure with single retry
#   docs(repo): define git discipline and branching model
#   chore(deps): bump playwright to 1.44.0
#   feat(agent)!: change ActionPlan schema (BREAKING CHANGE)
#
# BREAKING CHANGE example:
#   feat(planner)!: switch ActionPlan reasoning to structured object
#
#   BREAKING CHANGE: ActionPlan.reasoning is now { summary, steps }.
#
# ------------------ END TEMPLATE ------------------
